1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:09,598
At 12:15 AM on September 26, 1983, a red siren illuminated a top-secret Soviet bunker outside Moscow.

2
00:00:09,548 --> 00:00:16,791
The radar screens confirmed what every officer dreaded: five American nuclear warheads were already in the air.

3
00:00:16,791 --> 00:00:27,538
Soviet protocol gave Lieutenant Colonel Stanislav Petrov exactly twenty minutes to authorize a retaliatory strike that would wipe three hundred million people off the face of the Earth.

4
00:00:27,538 --> 00:00:31,971
pausa: 2s) The machine demanded retaliation.

5
00:00:31,971 --> 00:00:35,850
The satellite algorithms swore the missiles were real.

6
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,569
He had a direct line to the Kremlin.

7
00:00:38,569 --> 00:00:42,010
His finger hovered over the confirmation switch.

8
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:44,716
But instead of following orders...

9
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:49,149
pausa: 2s) Petrov decided to trust a hunch.

10
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:54,896
If the United States was going to start World War Three... why send only five missiles?

